    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full suite is green: **262 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented idempotent owner creation in `OwnerRestControllerV1` so that a repeated `POST /api/owners` carrying an already-seen `Idempotency-Key` header returns the originally created owner with `200 OK` instead of creating a duplicate.\n\nSince `addOwner` is defined by the OpenAPI-generated `OwnersApi` interface (which only passes `OwnerFieldsDto`), I read the header from the active request rather than altering the generated spec:\n\n- **Header access** \u2014 `currentIdempotencyKey()` reads the `Idempotency-Key` header via `RequestContextHolder`/`ServletRequestAttributes`, treating null/blank as absent.\n- **Key store** \u2014 a `ConcurrentHashMap<String, Integer>` (`idempotentCreations`) maps each seen key to the id of the owner it created.\n- **Replay path** \u2014 at the very start of `addOwner`, if the key is already recorded and its owner still exists, the method returns that owner's DTO (with `householdSize`/`bulkSignupWarning` populated the same way `getOwner` does) with `200 OK` \u2014 short-circuiting before the duplicate/identity checks that would otherwise return `409`.\n- **Record path** \u2014 after a successful `saveOwner`, the key is associated with the new owner's id (still returning `201 CREATED` on first create).\n\nThe new `AcceptanceTest.coreIdempotentRepeat` passes (same id returned, second call is `200`), and all 262 existing tests remain green. The store is keyed uniquely per request key, and a defensive null-check on the looked-up owner means a rolled-back/deleted owner simply falls through to a normal create.",
