    "probe_text": "Here is the complete, ordered account of what happens on `POST /api/owners`, based on `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` (`src/main/java/.../rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java:492`) plus the constraints that fire before the method body runs.\n\n## Before the method body\n\n1. **Authorization** \u2014 `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")`. Caller must have the `OWNER_ADMIN` role.\n2. **Bean Validation** on the `@Valid @RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto` (constraints from the generated DTO). A failure here yields a 400 before any controller code runs:\n   - `firstName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern(^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}$)`, `@Size(1..30)`\n   - `lastName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern(^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}\\.?$)`, `@Size(1..30)`\n   - `city` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern((?s).*\\S.*)` (non-blank), `@Size(1..80)`\n   - `telephone` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..20)`\n   - `address` \u2014 `@Pattern` (non-blank), `@Size(1..255)`\n   - `addressLine1` / `addressLine2` \u2014 `@Size(max 255)` each\n   - `title` \u2014 `@Size(max 10)`; `email` \u2014 `@Size(max 255)`\n\n## Inside the method (in execution order)\n\n3. **Idempotency short-circuit** \u2014 if an `Idempotency-Key` header is present and already maps to an existing owner, that owner is returned as **200 OK** (with `householdSize` and `bulkSignupWarning` recomputed) and **nothing new is created**.\n4. **Telephone normalization/validation** \u2014 `toE164()` strips spaces/dashes/brackets, applies `+61` default and national-length rules; if it can't produce a valid 8\u201315-digit E.164 number \u2192 **400**.\n5. **Email syntax** \u2014 if `email` is non-null and fails `EMAIL_PATTERN` \u2192 **400**.\n6. **Disposable email domain** \u2014 if the email's domain is on the blocklist \u2192 **400**.\n7. **Address resolution & presence** \u2014 normalizes `addressLine1`/`addressLine2` (structured form preferred) or else the flat `address`; if the resulting composed address is empty \u2192 **400**.\n8. **Postcode validity** \u2014 if `postcode` is non-null, `isPostcodeValid(postcode, city)` requires 4 digits and, when the city maps to a known region, requires the postcode to fall in that region's range \u2192 else **400**.\n9. **Registration date not in the future** \u2014 if `registrationDate` is provided and is after today \u2192 **400**.\n10. **Business-day roll-forward** \u2014 effective date (provided date, else today) is rolled forward past weekends/holidays via `toBusinessDay()`.\n11. **Daily creation cap** \u2014 counts existing owners whose registration date (as business day) equals this one; if `>= 100` \u2192 **429 Too Many Requests**.\n12. **Per-city cap** \u2014 counts existing owners in the same normalized city; if `>= 50` \u2192 **409 Conflict**.\n13. **Household duplicate** \u2014 computes a deterministic `householdId` from (normalized last name, postcode); if non-deleted owners already exist in that household and the request did **not** set `sharesHousehold` \u2192 **409**.\n14. **Identity uniqueness** \u2014 computes an `identityKey` from (E.164 telephone, email, householdId); if any non-deleted owner already has the same key \u2192 **409**.\n15. **Namesake count** \u2014 counts existing owners with the same normalized first+last name (used to populate a field, not a rejection).\n\n## Side-effects on success\n\n16. Maps DTO \u2192 `Owner`, then sets: `namesakeCount`; composed normalized `address`; `addressLine1`/`addressLine2` (or nulls when flat form used); E.164 `telephone`; lower-cased `email` (or null); business-day `registrationDate`.\n17. **Customer code** \u2014 `deduplicateCustomerCode(nextCustomerCode(region, telephone, lastName))`: region-prefixed SHA-256 hash, with `-<n>` suffix appended if it collides with an existing code.\n18. Sets `householdId`; sets `possibleDuplicateOf(null)`.\n19. **Persists** the owner via `clinicService.saveOwner(owner)`.\n20. If an `Idempotency-Key` was supplied, records `key \u2192 owner.id` in the idempotency map.\n21. Sets `householdSize`; writes an **audit log** line (id, customerCode, registrationDate, membership level/number).\n22. Maps to `OwnerDto`, sets `bulkSignupWarning` (`ownersCreatedThatDay > 80`), sets the `Location: /api/owners/{id}` header, and returns **201 Created**.\n\nNote the ordering nuance: the idempotency replay (step 3) happens *before* any field validation, while the `sharesHousehold` flag only bypasses the household-duplicate check (step 13), not the separate identity-uniqueness check (step 14)."
